You see the image of Gwenhyver making love to Launcelot, but it is only a mirage created from your inner fears in your fevered state.	你看見昆海兒與蘭斯洛特相擁纏綿的景象，但那不過是海市蜃樓，出自你發熱昏沉中內心的恐懼。
The mirage takes the shapes of Gwenhyver and Launcelot in a lovers' embrace.  This is a delusion, Arthur, caused by the torment of your own mind.	那幻象化作昆海兒與蘭斯洛特相擁的模樣。這只是幻覺，亞瑟，是你自己心神煎熬所致。
It is indeed an illusion, created by your own eyes, shaped by your fevered and tormented mind.	這確實只是幻覺，是你自己的眼睛所造，被你發熱煎熬的心神所形塑。
Your land and your people will die unless you fulfill your quest.  Do not give up.	除非你完成使命，否則你的國土與子民都將滅亡。莫要放棄。
Images shimmer and appear in the veils of rising heat.  It is Gwenhyver and Launcelot embracing.	影像在蒸騰的熱浪薄紗中閃爍浮現，是昆海兒與蘭斯洛特相擁的身影。
This image is but a vision of your own fears and jealousies, driven to the surface by your fevered, desperate brain.	這幅景象不過是你自身恐懼與嫉妒的幻象，被你發熱絕望的腦海逼上了表面。
Survival is more important than good taste, Arthur.	生存比講究品味更為要緊，亞瑟。
That was rather revolting, but at least the lizard's blood has revived you a tiny bit.	那滋味著實令人作嘔，但至少蜥蜴的血讓你稍稍回過了些氣力。
The lizard slipped past you.	那隻蜥蜴從你身邊溜走了。
Alas, you did not find water in time!  You die as parched as a piece of old leather, and soon your bones will adorn the sands.	唉，你未能及時尋得水源！你乾涸而死，如同一塊陳舊的皮革，不消多久，你的骸骨便將裝點這片沙地。
Alas, your strength failed and you died at the very edge of the water you so desperately needed. Truly, there is no justice in life.	唉，你的氣力耗盡，就死在你朝思暮想的水源近旁。人生當真毫無公道可言。
To add insult to injury, the scoundrel Jabir robs your corpse.	更教人氣憤的是，那無賴賈比耳竟洗劫了你的屍身。
That shimmer looks suspiciously like water.	那片閃爍，看起來很像是水。
It is indeed an illusion, created by your own eyes in the heat and thirst of the moment.	這確實只是幻覺，是你此刻酷熱難耐、口渴難當之下，自己的眼睛所造。
800 years before the birth of Christ, King Hezekiah ruled a city built on the large hill above this tunnel.	在基督誕生前八百年，希西家王統治著一座建於此地道上方大山丘上的城市。
The Assyrians were coming to attack the city, and the only source of water, the Spring of Gihon, lay before them at the base of the city.	亞述人正兵臨城下，而城中唯一的水源——基訓泉，就位於城基之前，正對著他們。
Hezekiah sent two teams of men to dig a tunnel.  One began at the Spring, the other from the opposite side of the hill.	希西家派遣兩隊人馬挖掘地道，一隊自泉源起工，另一隊則從山丘的另一側動工。
It is an amazing feat of that age that they dug through solid rock and met in the middle, thus forming this underground aqueduct.	他們鑿穿堅硬的岩石，在中途會合，造就了這條地下水道——這在當時堪稱驚人的工程壯舉。
The water flowed then from the Spring, which was covered over from sight, to the Pool of Siloam, hidden upon the far side of the hill.	泉水自此隱而不見，流經地道，直抵藏於山丘另一側的西羅亞池。
When the enemy arrived, they found no water and were forced to give up their seige.  Thus did King Hezekiah save his city.	敵軍抵達時遍尋不著水源，只得放棄圍城。希西家王便是如此保全了他的城池。
And yet, of that city no trace remains, and in its place the city now known as Jerusalem was built upon a larger hill to the north.	然而，那座城如今已不留一絲痕跡，取而代之的，是如今名為耶路撒冷的城市，建於北方一座更大的山丘之上。
If only you had a waterskin, but you do not.  You must drink your fill and reach Jerusalem as quickly as possible.	你若備有水袋就好了，可惜沒有。你必須在此暢飲個夠，並儘快趕往耶路撒冷。
They were foes of King Hezekiah.	他們是希西家王的敵人。
You may as well get started.  You have a long walk back.	你不妨這就動身，回程還有很長一段路要走。
It must be near.	想必就在附近。
You are under a hill at present.	你此刻正位於一座山丘之下。
The Spring of Gihon lies upon the far side of the large hill through which this aqueduct was dug.  It was hidden by King Hezekiah centuries ago.	基訓泉位於這座大山丘的另一側，這條水道正是穿山而鑿。數百年前，希西家王將它隱藏了起來。
The Pool of Siloam is fed by the Spring of Gihon through Hezekiah's Aqueduct.	西羅亞池的水源，正是透過希西家水道由基訓泉引來。
The cold water within this cool tunnel sends a shiver running through your body.	這條清涼地道裡的冰冷泉水，讓你渾身一陣寒顫。
The waters of the Pool of Siloam are cold and pure and fill you with relief.	西羅亞池的池水清冷純淨，讓你頓覺舒暢。
I fear the sight of you was too much for that poor girl.  She ran as though you were an evil djin.	恐怕是你的模樣把那可憐的女孩嚇壞了，她逃跑的樣子，彷彿把你當成了邪惡的精靈。
Such profane thoughts betray a moral weakness which may make you unworthy to find or possess the Grail.  You must control yourself.	如此褻瀆的念頭，暴露出你心志上的軟弱，恐怕會讓你失去尋得聖杯、持有聖杯的資格。你必須克制自己。
The girl, and her jug, have vanished over the hill.	那女孩連同她的水罐，已消失在山丘另一頭。
The girl has no interest in coming near you, let alone taking your money.	那女孩絲毫不想靠近你，更別說收下你的錢了。
She clearly has no desire to speak to you.	她顯然不想跟你說話。
The girl found you most frightening and wanted nothing to do with you.	那女孩覺得你十分嚇人，不想跟你有任何瓜葛。
The girl's jar was designed for carrying water.	那女孩的罐子是用來盛水的。
Do watch your step, Arthur.  You cannot afford to be careless.	亞瑟，走路留神些。你可經不起一時大意。
I doubt the natives will appreciate the mess you have made for them to clean up.  In your next life, do be more careful about where you step.	我看當地人未必會感激你留下這攤爛攤子讓他們收拾。下輩子，走路前可得看清楚些。
You are ignored, perhaps because you are obviously a 'foreign devil.'	沒人理睬你，或許是因為你一望即知是個「洋鬼子」。
No one is here.	此處無人。
I do not know of it.	我對此一無所知。
Never heard of him.	從未聽聞此人。
That brings you nothing but a look of confusion.	你這麼做，換來的只有一臉困惑。
They are here to look for thieves.	他們在此是為了緝查竊賊。
I am not certain who you mean.	我不確定你指的是誰。
It would be best to ask a merchant about the price of a certain thing.	若想知道某樣東西的價錢，最好去問商人。
I have nothing to say about him.	關於他，我無話可說。
I have nothing to say about her.	關於她，我無話可說。
Those who spend money are always welcome here.	願意花錢的人，在此永遠受歡迎。
You must not draw a weapon without good cause in this bazaar. The Muslims will not tolerate it and there are many of them and only one of you.	在這市集裡，切莫無故拔出武器。穆斯林絕不會容忍此事，況且他們人多勢眾，你孤身一人。
The apple works its spell. Your hunger and thirst vanish. The heaviness of your limbs is lightened.	這顆蘋果發揮了它的魔力。你的飢渴頓時消散，四肢的沉重也隨之減輕。
Often great wisdom and power may be hidden in a most ordinary guise.	偉大的智慧與力量，往往深藏在最平凡的外表之下。
Waste no time. Go to Fatima at once.	莫再耽擱，速速前去見法提瑪。
The Truth Spell of the Seeress provides you with the means to learn what a person wants. How you act upon that knowledge is the test placed before you.	女預言家的真言之術，能讓你窺知他人所求為何。至於如何運用這份洞悉，正是擺在你面前的試煉。
In Camelot, you may go anywhere you like, but not in Jerusalem.	在肯萊特，你可隨心所欲，任意通行；但在耶路撒冷卻不然。
Are you sure you have the right merchant for that?	你確定找對商人了嗎？
No-one answers to that title here.	此處無人以此稱謂應答。
She warned you it was delicate. Since you failed to eat it, it has fallen apart.	她警告過你這東西很脆弱。你既未及時吃下，它便已散壞。
You need to buy one, before you can eat it.	你得先買下一個，才能吃它。
I do not think she heard you.	我想她沒聽見你的話。
Most of it is written in Hebrew, of which I know very little.	這上頭大多以希伯來文寫成，我所知甚少。
I cannot quite tell precisely what the Hebrew graffiti says, but some of it, I believe, mentions dysentery.	我說不準這希伯來文塗鴉確切寫著什麼，但依我看，其中有些提到了痢疾。
"Habib" means simply "friend", but "habibi" is a warmer greeting, like saying "my friend".	「Habib」單純意為「朋友」，但「habibi」則是更親暱的問候語，如同說「我的朋友」。
Do not even consider it.	切莫存此念頭。
In this dangerous land, that would be as good as death.	在這險惡之地，那無異於尋死。
You are fit only to be a warrior in this land and Jerusalem has all the warriors it needs.	在此地，你唯一適合的身分是戰士，而耶路撒冷戰士已經足夠，不缺你一個。
You must use your wits if you hope to obtain money.	若盼望取得錢財，你得靠智謀行事。
Use carefully what you have. That is more important than how much you can accumulate.	善用你手頭所有之物，這比你能積攢多少更為重要。
That was a bloody waste.	那簡直是白白糟蹋。
That is beneath your dignity.	那有失你的尊嚴。
You have neither the means nor the need.	你既無此財力，也無此需要。
It is made of metal. You cannot break it.	它是金屬打造，你破壞不了。
It would not suit you.	那並不適合你。
I challenge you to find a use for this piece of cheap tin you have bought so dearly.	我倒要看看，你這花大錢買來的破錫片，究竟能派上什麼用場。
The birds already eat their fill from the grain merchant's spillage.	那些鳥兒早已從穀商灑落的穀粒中吃得飽飽的。
It is a foolish man who scatters grain upon barren ground for no reason.	無故將穀粒撒在貧瘠之地，實乃愚人所為。
I do not think you would enjoy eating raw grain.	我想你不會喜歡生嚼穀粒的滋味。
Eat raw meat? In THIS climate? I think not.	生吃肉？在這種氣候底下？我看還是免了。
First, you must have money.	首先，你得有錢才行。
You should be able to find what you need within this bazaar.	你所需要的東西，這市集裡應該找得到。
The many and varied smells of Jerusalem are, uhm, interesting, to say the least.	耶路撒冷這五花八門的氣味，嗯，至少可以說是別有一番趣味。
Nay! Jerusalem is ruled by the laws of Islam where they will cut off the hand of a thief.	不可！耶路撒冷奉行伊斯蘭律法，竊賊在此是要被斬去手掌的。
Do not be disgusting.	休得如此噁心。
Sa'alam aleikem. Peace be unto you.	Sa'alam aleikem. 願平安與你同在。
How can you tell a man is a hierophant merely by looking? You must seek words or deeds for such a judgment.	你怎能單憑外表便看出一人是祭司？要下此判斷，得從言語或行止中尋找端倪。
It is a word from ancient Greece meaning one who has knowledge of sacred mysteries.	這是源自古希臘的字眼，意指通曉神聖奧秘之人。
The gutter which runs down the center of the Street of David is most unsavory.	大衛街正中央那條水溝，氣味著實難聞。
The water in the gutter is unfit for any use.	水溝裡的水，什麼用途都派不上。
The street is paved of ancient stones, many hundreds of years older than Camelot.	這條街道由古老的石塊鋪成，比肯萊特還要年長上好幾百歲。
Nearly all of Jerusalem is made of the same, buff- coloured stone.	耶路撒冷幾乎清一色由同一種淺褐色的石塊建成。
The walls are mainly of the buff-coloured stone predominant here, or brick and plaster.	這裡的牆多半以當地常見的淺褐色石塊砌成，也有磚造與灰泥牆面。
There is nothing unusual about it.	這東西並無異常之處。
You mean that girl with the cage of doves? Pretty little thing, was she not?	你是說那個帶著鴿籠的女孩？生得挺俊俏的，不是嗎？
What girl? Did I miss something?	什麼女孩？我是不是錯過了什麼？
The coins of Jerusalem are the dinar which is gold, the dirham which is silver, and the fals which is copper.	耶路撒冷通行的錢幣有三種：金幣、銀幣，以及銅幣。
I can add nothing more to what you already know.	你已知曉之事，我再無可補充。
I shall know who and what she is when you do.	待你查明她是誰、是何身分之時，我自然也就知曉了。
You are not standing near that merchant.	你並未站在那位商人附近。
The city guards roam the bazaar, restless for any excuse to use their swords.	城中衛兵在市集裡巡邏遊走，一逮到藉口便迫不及待要拔劍。
You no longer have a purse, Arthur. You are alone in a strange city in a distant land without so much as a single copper coin.	亞瑟，你已沒有錢囊了。你孤身一人，身處異地陌生的城市，連一枚銅板都不剩。
I doubt if that thief would dare to show his face here again.	我看那賊人不敢再在此地露面了。
I have said all I ever care to say about the mule.	關於那頭騾子，我該說的都已說完。
She continues to follow you.	她仍舊跟隨著你。
She was with you when you entered Jerusalem. You had better look for her.	你進入耶路撒冷時，她本與你同行。你最好找找她的下落。
It is a common form of headdress in such a hot climate.	在這般炎熱的氣候下，這是常見的頭飾樣式。
The sun bakes the streets of Jerusalem.	烈日烤炙著耶路撒冷的街道。
Please attempt to control this rampage of excessive generosity.	還請你克制一下這股揮金如土的衝動。
I do not think that will be of interest to this merchant. Usually merchants wish to sell, not buy.	我想這位商人不會感興趣。商人通常是想賣東西，而非買東西。
You must have a buyer first.	你得先找到買家才行。
I do not have that for sale.	這東西我沒有要賣。
Difficult, since you are not dealing with anyone at the moment.	難辦，因為你此刻並未與任何人交易。
It might be of better use elsewhere.	這東西放在別處，或許更能派上用場。
That would be cruel, Arthur.	那未免太過殘忍了，亞瑟。
Kus em'ak.	Kus em'ak.
Yesh l'cha chara l'sechel.	Yesh l'cha chara l'sechel.
Ta'sim et ze b'tachat!	Ta'sim et ze b'tachat!
Ta'chel chara.	Ta'chel chara.
The doves are safely in their cage.	鴿子已安然待在籠中。
There are some doves up on the awning above you.	你頭頂的遮篷上，停著幾隻鴿子。
There are some doves up on the awning and balcony above you.	你頭頂的遮篷與陽台上，停著幾隻鴿子。
They are in the cage. You have caught them all.	牠們都在籠子裡了，你已經全數捉齊。
You would be taken for a lunatic if you stood here making bird calls.	你若站在這裡學鳥叫，旁人只會當你是個瘋子。
How bitterly this poor girl weeps! She is much distressed.	這可憐的女孩哭得好傷心！她十分苦惱。
She waits for you to follow her advice.	她等著你依她的話去做。
Six doves sit in the cage.	籠裡棲著六隻鴿子。
The cage is empty.	籠子空無一物。
Your tasks are done. Go now to the Seeress, for she awaits you.	你的任務已了。去見女預言家吧，她正等著你。
The poor girl is crying too much to speak again.	那可憐的女孩哭得說不出話來。
Money will not solve this poor girl's problem.	金錢解決不了這可憐女孩的難題。
